---
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import guide from '../../data/100-dollar-ai.json';
const r=guide.receipt;
const usd=(n:number)=>n.toLocaleString('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD'});
const count=(n:number)=>n.toLocaleString('en-US');
const elapsed=((new Date(r.counterCutoffAt).getTime()-new Date(r.commissionedAt).getTime())/60000).toFixed(1);
const base='/experiments/ai-100/';
const jsonLd={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article',headline:guide.title,description:guide.dek,datePublished:guide.asOf,author:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Codex — PointCast'},editor:{'@type':'Person',name:'Mike Hoydich'},publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'PointCast'},image:'https://pointcast.xyz'+base+'hero.png',mainEntityOfPage:'https://pointcast.xyz/reviews/100-dollar-ai'};
---
<BlockLayout title={guide.title} description={guide.dek} image={base+'hero.png'} jsonLd={jsonLd} immersive>
<main class="challenge">
<nav class="mast" aria-label="PointCast"><a href="/">POINTCAST <span>/ FIELD TEST</span></a><a href="/reviews">Reviews ↗</a><a href="/shop/front">Shop ↗</a></nav>
<header class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE $100 AI CHALLENGE / SEPTEMBER 2026</p><h1>Make<br/>it <em>real.</em></h1><p class="dek">Five assignments. Five things you can open. An honest look at the work, the bill, and the difference.</p><p class="byline">Editorial direction: <strong>Mike Hoydich</strong><br/>Built, checked & written by Codex · GPT-6 Astra</p><a class="button" href="#outputs">Open the work ↓</a></div><aside class="receipt"><p class="eyebrow">THE FIRST RECEIPT</p><div><span>Target ceiling</span><strong>$100</strong></div><div class="receipt-total"><span>API-equivalent at checkpoint</span><strong>{usd(r.apiEquivalentUsd)}</strong></div><div><span>Actual billed cost</span><strong>Unknown</strong></div><p>This is a standard-rate estimate from observed token counts, <strong>not an invoice</strong>. Existing access was used. Tool fees, hosting, human time and later publication work are excluded.</p><a href="#ledger">Inspect the calculation ↗</a></aside></header>
<div class="ribbon"><span>05 OPENABLE OUTPUTS</span><span>01 CONTINUING SESSION</span><span>00 NEW PURCHASES INITIATED</span></div>
<section class="section intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM THE PLAN TO THE THING</p><h2>Less “imagine if.”<br/>More “try it.”</h2></div><div><p>After our <a href="/reviews/ai-work-life">AI plans guide</a>, the next question was practical: what happens when you ask the tools to finish something?</p><p>Mike approved a $100 challenge with five assignments. Codex built a fictional brand kit, a small app, a document-reading exercise, a weekend plan and a short film. Every output is linked below. The acceptance rules were written before artifact production.</p><p>The budget experiment has a qualification up front: this session did not expose a per-task invoice. We can show a <strong>{usd(r.apiEquivalentUsd)} API-equivalent checkpoint</strong>, not claim that the entire project cost that amount—or prove an all-in result under $100.</p><p>The work is still inspectable. That is the useful part.</p></div></section>
<section id="outputs" class="section outputs"><p class="eyebrow">THE FIVE ASSIGNMENTS</p><h2>Open the evidence.</h2><div class="jump-links">{guide.items.map(i=><a href={'#'+i.id}>{i.number} / {i.type}</a>)}</div>{guide.items.map(i=><article class="assignment" id={i.id}><div class="assignment-label"><span>{i.number}</span><p class="eyebrow">{i.type}</p><p class="status">{i.status}</p></div><div class="assignment-body"><h3>{i.name}</h3><p class="brief"><strong>The brief.</strong> {i.brief}</p><p>{i.result}</p><div class="evidence"><div><h4>What was checked</h4><p>{i.check}</p></div><div><h4>What this does not prove</h4><p>{i.limit}</p></div></div><p class="take">{i.take}</p><a class="button" href={base+i.file}>Open output {i.number} ↗</a>{i.id==='app'&&<a class="secondary" href={base+'split-core.mjs'}>Inspect the calculation source</a>}{i.id==='document'&&<a class="secondary" href={base+'room-memo.txt'}>Read the complete source memo</a>}{i.id==='short'&&<div class="video-wrap"><video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster={base+'short-poster.png'} aria-label="One Good Hour, a 20-second silent short"><source src={base+'one-good-hour.mp4'} type="video/mp4"/></video><div><p class="eyebrow">THE FEED CAN WAIT / 20 SECONDS</p><p>A tiny film for the fictional brand. Press play; there is no audio.</p><p>Transcript: “One Good Hour.” “Find ten blue things.” “Draw a terrible pear.” “Ask one better question.” “The feed can wait.”</p><a href={base+'one-good-hour.mp4'} download>Download the MP4 ↗</a><p class="fine">Original type and shapes, rendered from AI-authored code. This is not a review of a text-to-video model.</p></div></div>}</div></article>)}</section>
<section class="section observations"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT CHANGED ALONG THE WAY</p><h2>The useful friction.</h2><div class="two">{guide.fixes.map(f=><article><h3>{f.label}</h3><p>{f.detail}</p></article>)}</div><p class="fine">No dramatic failure story has been manufactured. The automated bill-splitter tests passed on their first recorded run. These notes describe observed limits and actual agent revisions.</p></section>
<section id="ledger" class="section ledger"><div class="ledger-intro"><p class="eyebrow">THE ACCOUNTING, WITHOUT THE MAGIC TRICK</p><h2>{usd(r.apiEquivalentUsd)} is a proxy.<br/>Not the bill.</h2><p class="lead">The headline budget was $100. The measured checkpoint is below that at standard API rates. The actual all-in cost remains unverified.</p></div><div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Token cost calculation"><table><caption>Observed session-counter delta × published standard GPT-6 Astra rates</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Meter</th><th scope="col">Tokens</th><th scope="col">Per million</th><th scope="col">Equivalent</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Uncached input</th><td>{count(r.uncachedInputTokens)}</td><td>$10.00</td><td>{usd(r.uncachedInputTokens*10/1e6)}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cached input</th><td>{count(r.usageDelta.cached_input_tokens)}</td><td>$1.00</td><td>{usd(r.usageDelta.cached_input_tokens/1e6)}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Output, including reasoning</th><td>{count(r.usageDelta.output_tokens)}</td><td>$50.00</td><td>{usd(r.usageDelta.output_tokens*50/1e6)}</td></tr><tr class="total"><th scope="row">Total before display rounding</th><td colspan="2">${r.apiEquivalentUsd.toFixed(6)}</td><td>{usd(r.apiEquivalentUsd)}</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="fine">No cache-write tokens were recorded. Reasoning output is already included in the output total and is not counted twice. Rates checked September 29, 2026: <a href={r.rateSource}>official model rate card ↗</a>. <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/token-counting">How output token accounting works ↗</a>.</p><div class="two ledger-notes"><article><h3>Why so much cached input?</h3><p>This ran inside an existing conversation. The input total counts context sent repeatedly, including earlier conversation material. About {(r.usageDelta.cached_input_tokens/r.usageDelta.input_tokens*100).toFixed(1)}% of recorded input was cached. A clean session, another plan or a different model can behave differently.</p><p>For a sensitivity check, pricing all recorded input as uncached would produce <strong>{usd((r.usageDelta.input_tokens*10+r.usageDelta.output_tokens*50)/1e6)}</strong> for the same token counts. That is another hypothetical, not an observed second run.</p></article><article><h3>What is inside the checkpoint?</h3><p>The counter window spans <strong>{elapsed} minutes</strong>, from commission through the recorded artifact-acceptance checkpoint. It includes research, setup and artifact work in this session. It is elapsed clock time, not measured model-only runtime or human labor saved.</p><p>Article assembly, later checks, deployment, tool fees, hosting, electricity and human time are outside this figure. No new subscription, API credit purchase or checkout was initiated. Existing access is not free just because no purchase happened here.</p></article></div><details><summary>Exact timestamps, scope and receipt</summary><p>Commission: <time datetime={r.commissionedAt}>{r.commissionedAt}</time><br/>Observed token cutoff: <time datetime={r.counterCutoffAt}>{r.counterCutoffAt}</time>. Times are UTC; the work was commissioned September 29 in Los Angeles.</p><p>{r.scope}</p><p>The estimate applies standard public API rates to observed Codex session usage. It is not the account’s billing tier or a verified charge. Usage counters are reported by the local session; no private transcript or credentials are published.</p><a href={base+'receipt.json'}>Download the numeric receipt ↗</a> · <a href={base+'events.json'}>Read the timestamped work log ↗</a></details></section>
<section class="section verdict"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT WE WOULD PAY FOR AGAIN</p><h2>The narrow job.<br/>The visible result.</h2><p class="lead">The clearest win here is the tiny app: it does one thing, and we can verify the cents. The brand kit is a useful starting point. The document and itinerary are valuable only when their sources and gaps stay attached. The short is finished, but “finished” does not mean “effective advertising.”</p><p>The experiment shows that one assistant can turn several small briefs into inspectable artifacts in a single working session. It does not establish that AI replaces a designer, developer, lawyer, travel planner or filmmaker. We did not measure a human baseline, repeat the runs or compare models.</p><p>If you try this yourself, choose a task with a checkable finish line. Keep the brief, the original material, the result and the corrections. A folder of usable work is a better reason to pay than a folder of impressive promises.</p><div class="download"><a class="button" href={base+'outputs.zip'} download>Download all five outputs + source ↓</a><a href={base+'manifest.json'}>File hashes & sizes ↗</a><a href={base+'protocol.txt'}>Read the original acceptance rules ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section closing"><p class="eyebrow">POINTCAST / THE WORK IS OPEN</p><h2>Try it.<br/>Check it.<br/>Keep what helps.</h2><p>Commissioned by Mike Hoydich. Built and written by Codex, using GPT-6 Astra as reported by the session. This is a self-reviewed field demonstration with synthetic examples, not an independent benchmark. No sponsorship, affiliate links or fabricated customer results.</p><a href="/reviews/ai-work-life">Choose an AI plan →</a><a href="/reviews/ai-plans">Compare subscription tiers →</a><a href="/reviews/100-dollar-ai.json">Read this field test as JSON →</a><a href="/shop/front">Back to the shop →</a></section>
</main>
</BlockLayout>
<style>
:global(body){margin:0;background:#f6f2e9}.challenge{--ink:#172b25;--paper:#f6f2e9;--blue:#244dff;--lime:#e7f58b;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}.challenge *{box-sizing:border-box}.challenge a{color:inherit}.mast{display:flex;gap:25px;align-items:center;padding:24px 5vw;background:var(--ink);color:white;font-size:12px}.mast a{text-decoration:none}.mast a:first-child{margin-right:auto;font-size:21px;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-1px}.mast span{font:10px monospace;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--lime);margin-left:12px}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:65px;padding:65px 6vw;background:var(--blue);color:var(--paper);align-items:center}.eyebrow{font:700 11px/1.7 monospace;letter-spacing:1.6px;margin:0 0 25px}h1{font-size:clamp(84px,11vw,170px);line-height:.85;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:30px 0}h1 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--lime)}.dek{font-size:24px;line-height:1.4;max-width:30ch}.byline{font-size:12px;line-height:1.8;margin:25px 0}.button{display:inline-block;background:var(--ink);color:white!important;padding:17px 22px;text-decoration:none;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.5}.hero .button{background:var(--lime);color:var(--ink)!important}.receipt{background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);padding:32px;transform:rotate(2deg);box-shadow:10px 12px 0 #1430a5;border-bottom:9px dashed var(--blue)}.receipt>div{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px;padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px dashed #a7b0a4;font:13px/1.5 monospace}.receipt strong{font-size:19px}.receipt .receipt-total{display:block}.receipt-total strong{display:block;font:700 70px Arial;letter-spacing:-4px;margin-top:10px}.receipt p:not(.eyebrow){font-size:13px;line-height:1.7}.receipt p strong{font-size:13px}.receipt>a{font-size:12px;font-weight:700}.ribbon{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:22px 6vw;background:var(--lime);font:700 11px monospace}.section{padding:65px 6vw;max-width:1500px;margin:auto}h2{font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,68px);line-height:1.03;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:0 0 30px}p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.75}.intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:60px}.intro p:first-child{margin-top:0}.jump-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:30px 0 50px}.jump-links a{border:1px solid;padding:12px 15px;font:11px monospace;text-decoration:none}.assignment{display:grid;grid-template-columns:190px 1fr;gap:40px;border-top:3px solid var(--ink);padding:38px 0 55px;scroll-margin-top:20px}.assignment-label>span{font:700 90px Arial;letter-spacing:-6px}.assignment-label .eyebrow{margin:14px 0}.status{font:11px/1.7 monospace;max-width:17ch}.assignment h3{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,49px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-2px;margin:8px 0 25px}.brief{font-size:14px;color:#516152}.evidence{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:25px;background:#e8ecd9;padding:24px;margin:25px 0}.evidence h4{font:700 11px/1.6 monospace;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 10px}.evidence p{font-size:13px;margin:0}.take{font-size:22px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;border-left:4px solid var(--blue);padding-left:20px}.secondary{display:inline-block;margin:20px;font-size:12px}.video-wrap{display:grid;grid-template-columns:300px 1fr;gap:30px;margin-top:35px;align-items:center}.video-wrap video{width:100%;display:block;background:var(--ink)}.video-wrap p{font-size:14px}.video-wrap a{font-size:13px}.fine{font-size:12px!important;line-height:1.7;color:#526252}.two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px 45px}.two h3{font-size:24px;letter-spacing:-.6px}.two p{font-size:15px}.observations{background:#e8ecd9;max-width:none}.ledger{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);max-width:none}.ledger h2{color:var(--lime)}.lead{font-size:23px;line-height:1.5;max-width:65ch}.ledger .fine{color:#becbbc}.ledger-intro{max-width:1000px}.table-scroll{overflow:auto;margin:35px 0 20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;min-width:650px;width:100%;font-size:14px;text-align:left}caption{text-align:left;font:11px/1.7 monospace;margin-bottom:16px}th,td{padding:20px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #516151}td{font-family:monospace}thead{background:#2d4237}.total{color:var(--lime)}.ledger-notes{margin-top:35px}.ledger details{border-top:1px solid #516151;padding-top:24px;margin-top:30px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.7}.ledger details p{font-size:13px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700}.verdict>p{max-width:76ch}.download{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:25px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:35px}.download>a:not(.button){font-size:12px}.closing{background:var(--lime);max-width:none}.closing>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:70ch;font-size:14px}.closing>a{display:inline-block;margin:20px 25px 0 0;font-size:13px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible,video:focus-visible,.table-scroll:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ff7950;outline-offset:5px}
@media(max-width:950px){.hero{gap:30px}.receipt{padding:25px}.assignment{grid-template-columns:120px 1fr;gap:25px}.video-wrap{grid-template-columns:220px 1fr}.intro{gap:30px}}
@media(max-width:700px){.mast{padding:20px;gap:16px}.mast span{display:none}.mast a:first-child{font-size:18px}.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:38px 24px 45px;gap:35px}.hero h1{font-size:100px}.dek{font-size:22px}.receipt{transform:none;margin-right:8px}.ribbon{display:grid;padding:22px 24px;gap:14px}.section{padding:43px 24px}.intro,.two,.assignment,.evidence,.video-wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr}.assignment{gap:10px;padding-top:25px}.assignment-label{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:15px}.assignment-label>span{font-size:48px;letter-spacing:-3px}.assignment-label .eyebrow{margin:0}.assignment-label .status{max-width:none;width:100%;margin:0 0 10px}.assignment h3{letter-spacing:-1px}.evidence{gap:25px;padding:20px}.secondary{margin:20px 0 0;display:block}.video-wrap video{max-width:340px}.take{font-size:21px}.lead{font-size:20px}.download{gap:20px}.receipt-total strong{font-size:64px}}
</style>
